1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:05,130
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:16,808
[Dante] <i>This is going to be our new home!</i>

3
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,978
[Camia] <i>No one will think</i>
<i>of doing us harm here.</i>

4
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:24,482
[Julio] <i>As long as this statue</i>
<i>stands firm in our town,</i>

5
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:29,279
<i>you will continue to have</i>
<i>honest service and leadership.</i>

6
00:00:29,362 --> 00:00:30,697
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

7
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,532
[all] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

8
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,200
[young Diego] <i>No one in</i>
<i>the Ardiente family is weak.</i>

9
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,535
<i>Hey, don't jump!</i>

10
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:37,245
[screaming]

11
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:39,330
[young Diego] <i>Teacher Camia is helping me.</i>

12
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:42,083
<i>She's my new friend Lily's mom.</i>

13
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,085
<i>-Raul, stay away!</i>
<i>-Is it so wrong</i>

14
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:45,545
<i>-to be friends with you?</i>
<i>-Stay away!</i>

15
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:47,046
[Camia] <i>Go away! Get your hands off me!</i>

16
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,548
<i>Please, stop!</i>

17
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,008
<i>Your position doesn't scare me,</i>

18
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:51,843
<i>even if you think you own this town!</i>

19
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:55,221
[Camia] <i>You killed my husband! Get out!</i>

20
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:56,514
[Emilia] <i>You know what to do with her.</i>

21
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,933
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

22
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:00,435
[gunshot]

23
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:04,898
[theme music continues]

24
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:08,860
<i>I want justice for my mom and dad!</i>

25
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,612
<i>I've legally adopted you.</i>

26
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:12,947
<i>You'll be called Ivy Aguas.</i>

27
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:16,743
[Ivy] <i>This was the only way</i>
<i>for me to be reborn.</i>

28
00:01:16,826 --> 00:01:18,828
<i>To become a new me.</i>

29
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:24,501
[Prianka] <i>Do what you must do.</i>
<i>Make them pay.</i>

30
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:25,460
WELCOME TO POBLACION ARDIENTE

31
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:29,339
[Ivy] <i>I want you to remember my face.</i>

32
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:34,427
<i>I am Ivy Aguas, and I am vengeance.</i>

33
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:39,349
[Julio] <i>These things started</i>
<i>the moment she came here.</i>

34
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:43,311
[Loring] <i>How could you</i>
<i>let this happen to your son?!</i>

35
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:46,397
[Ivy] <i>Mom? Mom? It's me.</i>
<i>Mom, it's me, Lily.</i>

36
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:50,902
[Diego] <i>Are Ivy Aguas</i>
<i>and Lily Cruz the same person?</i>

37
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:53,530
<i>Yes, Diego. I'm your old friend.</i>

38
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:56,074
[Camia] <i>If you're going</i>
<i>to fight the Ardientes,</i>

39
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:57,534
<i>then I'll fight with you.</i>

40
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:01,788
[Julio] <i>Arnaldo, you are the man!</i>

41
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:02,997
<i>If not for you,</i>

42
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:05,166
<i>your parents would've been imprisoned now,</i>

43
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:09,504
<i>and all of us Ardientes</i>
<i>would have lost our reputation.</i>

44
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:11,798
[Diego] <i>As long as the</i>
<i>Ardientes are in power,</i>

45
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:13,091
<i>they can't be brought down.</i>

46
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:15,051
<i>Someone should fight them head-on.</i>

47
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:16,678
<i>I'll run for governor.</i>

48
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:20,682
<i>Ivy!</i>

49
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:22,976
-[Arnaldo screaming]
-[Carlotta gasping]

50
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:25,728
[screaming, sobbing]

51
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:28,314
[Rufo] <i>Tell the congressman</i>
<i>that the Jaguar is here.</i>

52
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:30,441
<i>And he will rule Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

53
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:34,696
[Ivy] <i>What do you have to do</i>
<i>with Nanny Carlotta's death?</i>

54
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:36,281
[gunshots]

55
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:37,949
[Ivy] <i>Everything will be over soon.</i>

56
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:39,784
<i>This town will finally be free</i>

57
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:42,036
<i>from the Ardiente family's grip.</i>

58
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,621
<i>Stop the wedding!</i>

59
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:44,873
[Arnaldo] <i>I can easily kill you,</i>

60
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,541
<i>like what I did to Carlotta.</i>

61
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:47,917
<i>I didn't mean to.</i>

62
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:49,627
<i>Monster!</i>

63
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:51,713
<i>-I didn't mean it!</i>
<i>-You bastard!</i>

64
00:02:51,796 --> 00:02:53,298
-[Diego] <i>Ivy!</i>
-[Raul] <i>Let go of my son!</i>

65
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:54,674
-[guests screaming]
-[gunshot]

66
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,509
<i>Lily!</i>

67
00:02:56,593 --> 00:03:00,346
-[screaming]
-[gunshots]

68
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,764
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I'm right here.</i>

69
00:03:04,559 --> 00:03:05,768
<i>We did it.</i>

70
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:08,938
<i>Ivy?</i>

71
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:11,566
<i>Ivy!</i>

72
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:16,362
[suspenseful music playing]

73
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:25,288
-[clamoring]
-[Arnaldo] Hey! Hey!

74
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:26,915
-[man 1] Chief! Chief!
-[man 2] Arrest him!

75
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:27,957
[clamoring]

76
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,542
[man 3] You monster!

77
00:03:29,792 --> 00:03:31,252
[man 4] Serves you right.

78
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:33,296
Arrest him! Arrest him!

79
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:34,213
[Arnaldo] No!

80
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,757
-[Marlon] Rot in jail!
-[Arnaldo] No!

81
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,800
-[Marlon] You'll rot in there!
-[man 5] Murderer!

82
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,135
[Fernan] You deserve to die!

83
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,428
-[Marlon] Murderer!
-[Fernan] Serves you right!

84
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:43,223
Don't touch me! I'm still the mayor here.

85
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:44,766
-Move! Move! Move!
-[Julio] Move!

86
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:46,351
-Grandpa! Grandpa!
-[Julio] Get out of my way!

87
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:47,352
[Arnaldo] You're going to regret this!

88
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,062
-[Raul] Move! Move!
-[man 6] Murderer!

89
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,480
-Grandpa, what's this?!
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!

90
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:52,899
[clamoring]

91
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:55,026
[Fernan] You're a family of criminals!

92
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:57,320
-Criminals, are we?
-[Arnaldo] Let me go!

93
00:03:57,403 --> 00:03:59,155
You think you're actually right?

94
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:05,161
Aren't you aware that what
you did is against the law?!

95
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:09,249
You can't arrest the mayor and hurt him!

96
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:11,709
You don't have the authority to do that!

97
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:15,213
Do you have a warrant
of arrest to seize him

98
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:16,297
and bring him here?!

99
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:21,344
Whoever your ringleader is
has really led you all on!

100
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:24,806
All of you can be
arrested and sent to jail!

101
00:04:25,181 --> 00:04:26,724
You have no right to be self-righteous!

102
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:30,144
[tense music playing]

103
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:32,230
[music fades]

104
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:33,189
-[Camia sobbing] Lily!
-[Diego] Auntie.

105
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:35,441
Diego, what happened to my daughter?

106
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:38,236
Is she badly hurt? Answer me! [sobbing]

107
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:41,239
She was hit in the shoulder,
but don't worry.

108
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:43,366
The doctors are doing their best.

109
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:46,452
Where is the bastard
who did this to my daughter?

110
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:51,124
Bring me Arnaldo!
I want to see him this instant!

111
00:04:51,207 --> 00:04:52,875
Aunt Camia, calm down.

112
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:55,086
We'll make him pay…

113
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,713
for everything he did.

114
00:04:57,171 --> 00:05:01,092
So please calm down.
Lily's going to be okay.

115
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:03,803
[Camia sobbing]

116
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:12,437
-[Fernan] Murderer!
-[Arnaldo] I'm not a murderer!

117
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:14,063
Quiet down!

118
00:05:14,147 --> 00:05:15,106
[clamoring]

119
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:16,316
You're monsters!

120
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:18,109
That's enough!

121
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:19,861
[Julio] What do you really want?!

122
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:21,571
You want Arnaldo to go to jail?!

123
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,698
[in unison] Yes! He should be in jail!

124
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,867
-That's not going to happen!
-[Marlon] Jail him!

125
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:26,951
[Arnaldo] That's not going to happen!

126
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,870
-Chief!
-[man 7] Murderer!

127
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:30,705
-Put Arnaldo behind bars.
-[crowd] Yeah!

128
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:32,832
-[crowd cheering, applauding]
-[scoffs]

129
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:35,376
Grandpa! No! No! No! No! No! No!

130
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,211
-Take him now!
-[Marlon] That's right!

131
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:39,714
-Dad! Dad! Mom! Mom!
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!

132
00:05:39,797 --> 00:05:40,757
[Arnaldo] Dad!

133
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:45,470
[crowd whooping, applauding]

134
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:46,929
Pa, what is this?

135
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:49,015
Emilia, I know what I'm doing.

136
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,392
[man 8] For the new Ardiente!

137
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,145
Do you see how furious
those people are, Chief?

138
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:56,522
[Julio] The reason why I
agreed to put Arnaldo in jail

139
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,691
is because you might not
be able to control them.

140
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:01,736
They'll barge in and hurt my grandson,

141
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:04,489
-or worse, kill him.
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

142
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:07,784
-Now that Arnaldo's behind bars,
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

143
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:10,661
-and he's under your custody,
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

144
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,372
-I'll hold you responsible…
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

145
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,832
[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

146
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,751
-if anything bad happens to him!
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

147
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:18,461
-[Julio] Is that clear?!
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

148
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:20,713
-Yes, Congressman.
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

149
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,924
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!
-[Emilia] Papa.

150
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:24,467
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!
-Look at them!

151
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:27,053
-For the new Ardiente!
-For the new Ardiente!

152
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:29,180
-Look at those imbeciles.
-Diego! Diego! Diego!

153
00:06:29,263 --> 00:06:33,643
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

154
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:34,727
Let them enjoy this moment.

155
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:37,438
But in the end, we'll have the last laugh.

156
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:41,150
Mark my words. I'll make
them cry tears of blood!

157
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,860
[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

158
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:46,364
My grandson won't rot in prison…

159
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:49,158
-and all of them will realize…
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

160
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:52,286
-what a huge mistake it was…
-[crowd] Diego! Diego! Diego!

161
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:54,330
to go against the Ardientes!

162
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:57,750
-[man 9] For change!
-Enjoy it while it lasts, fools!

163
00:06:57,834 --> 00:07:03,923
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

164
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:05,842
-[crowd] Diego!
-[man] For real change!

165
00:07:05,925 --> 00:07:08,219
[Camia] Please keep my daughter safe.

166
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:13,099
[sobbing]

167
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:15,893
Auntie, I have to go.

168
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:20,106
Nanny Loring, Uncle Pandoy.
Take care of everything here.

169
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:23,317
Diego. Where are you going?

170
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:28,948
What they've done to my
grandson is illegal confinement.

171
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:33,828
Arnaldo was not caught committing a crime

172
00:07:33,911 --> 00:07:35,913
or in the act of committing one.

173
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:39,292
He was not given due process.

174
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:42,211
Even his arrest was illegal

175
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:44,547
because there was no warrant served.

176
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:47,967
And the video of his alleged confession

177
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:49,802
is clearly tampered with.

178
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:52,513
So I don't see any reason

179
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:56,726
for my grandson not to be
released from jail immediately.

180
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:58,352
You're right, Congressman.

181
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:00,563
We can file a petition for habeas corpus

182
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:01,814
to dismiss the case.

183
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,065
[Julio] Good.

184
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,275
But, Julio…

185
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,236
A lot of people heard Arnaldo's confession

186
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,572
in front of Ivy at the wedding.

187
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:10,531
[laughs gently]

188
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:11,824
[Emilia] And, Papa, if that gets out

189
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,201
during the preliminary investigation…

190
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:14,911
the case will be heard in court.

191
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:19,165
It's simple, really. I have a solution.

192
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:23,878
Cut off the tongue of
anyone who tries to talk.

193
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:30,301
Slice off the ears of those
who will listen to them.

194
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:34,472
Have they forgotten
who they're up against?

195
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:36,641
We are the Ardientes.

196
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:42,313
We can break, bend,
or turn the law around…

197
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,440
to how we want it to.

198
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:51,948
We can also erase or alter any
evidence that they might have.

199
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,116
Jepoy, what are you doing? Stop it.

200
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,702
-What's happening to you?
-This is all my fault, Anna!

201
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:58,663
Arnaldo managed to snatch my gun.

202
00:08:58,746 --> 00:09:02,333
Of all people, he got mine!
[breathes heavily]

203
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:05,253
If I hadn't interfered with the plan,

204
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:06,587
this wouldn't have happened.

205
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,381
[Jepoy breathing heavily]

206
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:10,132
This is my fault, Anna.

207
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:12,552
Jepoy.

208
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:20,685
[breathing heavily]

209
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,482
[exhales]

210
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:28,693
Ivy is Lily Cruz.

211
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,029
She's my daughter.

212
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:38,786
She had to hide her identity to
exact revenge on the Ardientes.

213
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:43,583
Promise me that no one
will find out about it.

214
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,878
The Ardientes will kill Lily

215
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:50,590
if they find out the truth about her.

216
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:56,929
Yes, Camia. We promise.

217
00:09:58,389 --> 00:10:01,767
We will take this secret to our graves.

218
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:06,188
We're the only ones who can help
each other fight the Ardientes.

219
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:10,693
Thank you.

220
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:15,948
[dramatic music playing]

221
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:23,414
[reporter] <i>A citizen's arrest</i>
<i>was conducted by the people</i>

222
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:26,834
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente</i>
<i>against Mayor Arnaldo Torillo.</i>

223
00:10:26,917 --> 00:10:29,378
<i>This was after he confessed to killing</i>

224
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:31,380
<i>Carlotta Navarro and Nimfa Naig.</i>

225
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:33,424
[Emilia's hitman]
You won't get anything from me!

226
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:34,842
[man 1] Murderer!

227
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:39,472
[Diego] Put these men in jail
and arrest Emilia Torillo!

228
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:41,891
What is this all about?!

229
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:46,062
She attempted to have Ivy Aguas
killed to stop the wedding.

230
00:10:46,145 --> 00:10:46,896
Who, me?!

231
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,357
And they were also the ones
who planted the bomb.

232
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,026
You tried to stop the wedding?

233
00:10:52,109 --> 00:10:53,110
[Emilia] That's a lie!

234
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:54,904
I have the evidence.

235
00:10:55,696 --> 00:11:00,117
This contains records of phone
calls and text messages

236
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:02,912
between Emilia Torillo and her hitman.

237
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:05,373
Honestly, Diego!

238
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:07,917
Papa, why would you believe this bastard?

239
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:13,089
And how will you prove that the
number used is mine, pray tell?

240
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:20,346
Who ordered you?
Tell us who gave you orders!

241
00:11:21,013 --> 00:11:22,181
-Admit it!
-Admit it!

242
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:23,557
-Admit it!
-Speak up.

243
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,440
-The devil!
-[chuckles sarcastically]

244
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:34,151
[Emilia's hitman] It was the
devil who ordered me to do it!

245
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:37,196
-Liar! Liar!
-[man 2] Blaming it on the devil, eh?

246
00:11:37,279 --> 00:11:38,155
-Arrest him!
-[laughing]

247
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:40,032
-[police officer] Leave him to us!
-[man 2] Arrest him!

248
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:41,617
-[laughing]
-[Diego] Arrest him!

249
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,412
-[man 2] Give them the gun!
-[man 3] Here!

250
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:45,955
Nice try, Diego.

251
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:49,041
But, next time,
if you're looking for someone

252
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:51,877
to help you take us down,
don't search here.

253
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:54,505
Go find help in the dumpster,
where you belong!

254
00:11:54,588 --> 00:11:55,840
-They're liars.
-All of them.

255
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:58,426
Your family is the worst
piece of garbage there is!

256
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:08,978
And I'll make sure that
you'll pay for all your crimes.

257
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,188
Oh, really, Diego?

258
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,107
Then we're also going
to make sure that you go down.

259
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:18,320
You think I don't know that you
and Ivy planned to overthrow us?

260
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:20,739
Oh, stop it, Emilia!

261
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:25,578
Let's end this pointless little act!

262
00:12:25,911 --> 00:12:26,871
[Julio] You.

263
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:29,206
And all of you!

264
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:35,254
If any of you wish
to file cases against me

265
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:39,884
or any member of my family, go ahead!

266
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:43,012
It's your right. But let me warn you.

267
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:48,309
We will be ready to face
all your charges and allegations

268
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:52,771
at the proper time
and in the proper forum.

269
00:12:54,523 --> 00:12:58,319
Now, I do not need
any more of this aggravation!

270
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:03,949
Emilia. Raul. Let's go.

271
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:08,662
Let's put an end to this
third-rate circus act!

272
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:14,251
-[Fernan] Murderers!
-[man] Murderers!

273
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:15,753
Records say she's okay.

274
00:13:15,836 --> 00:13:17,421
I think she can go out in a few days.

275
00:13:17,505 --> 00:13:18,506
Okay.

276
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,633
-Hello.
-Hi, doc.

277
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:23,802
Ivy's condition is stable.

278
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:27,723
She's lucky the bullet
didn't hit her heart.

279
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:29,767
-Thank you, doc.
-[doctor] All right.

280
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:32,394
-Thank you.
-Excuse me. Excuse me.

281
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:33,646
[Loring] Thank you.

282
00:13:34,313 --> 00:13:38,776
[soft music playing]

283
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:42,905
Lily, dear…

284
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,533
I'm right here, okay?

285
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:48,536
I won't leave your side.

286
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:55,876
Let me out of here! Hey! Hey!

287
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:57,753
I'm the mayor of this place!

288
00:13:57,836 --> 00:14:00,381
Why are you keeping me in here?! [screams]

289
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:02,049
[thuds]

290
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:04,385
Let me out of here!

291
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,221
Hey! Shut it! You're so noisy!

292
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:08,931
-[thuds]
-What did you say?! Huh?!

293
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:11,433
You may be the boss in here,
but I'm the mayor.

294
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:14,019
Come here. Let me rub that back for you!

295
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,229
[laughs]

296
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:19,400
[scoffs] No! No!

297
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:20,901
[screaming]

298
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:24,446
[Arnaldo] No, no, no, no. No. No.

299
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:27,408
[groaning]

300
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:32,913
[tense music playing]

301
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:36,458
You did all this! You!

302
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:41,213
You ruined us! How could I let you?!

303
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:42,715
You're pathetic!

304
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:44,466
You and Ivy were ruined a long time ago.

305
00:14:45,342 --> 00:14:48,178
Since the day you killed Nanny Carlotta.

306
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:51,682
[tense music intensifies]

307
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:53,100
You'll rot in here.

308
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:58,939
And no matter what…

309
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:03,402
you will never get Ivy back.

310
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,782
[Arnaldo laughs]

311
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:10,326
You will rot in here.

312
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:13,162
[groans] Where's Ivy?

313
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:18,042
Tell me where she is.

314
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:20,461
I just want to know where she is.

315
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,880
Come on, tell me.

316
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:25,925
From one man to another,
it's lonely in here.

317
00:15:27,259 --> 00:15:29,553
Come on, just tell her
we have a honeymoon to do.

318
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:32,097
I'm the mayor. I'm loaded with money.

319
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:35,684
I can convert this cell into
a hotel room for all I care.

320
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:40,564
Just tell her, come on. Come on.
Please. I miss Ivy.

321
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:43,651
I miss everything about her.
I miss her body. I miss her.

322
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:46,987
I miss her lips. Please tell her, come on.

323
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:50,532
I miss her lips.
I miss everything about her.

324
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:57,081
Do you hear me? She's mine! Hey! Hey!

325
00:15:57,414 --> 00:16:00,042
She's mine! Diego!

326
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:04,463
[tense music intensifies]

327
00:16:04,546 --> 00:16:07,424
Grandpa! Mom!

328
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,678
[sobs]

329
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:13,305
[groans]

330
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:16,016
[door opens]

331
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:18,435
-Oh. Diego.
-Uncle.

332
00:16:19,853 --> 00:16:20,980
[quietly] Where did you go?

333
00:16:22,606 --> 00:16:23,565
Nanny.

334
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:25,442
Where have you been?

335
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,236
How's Ivy?

336
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:31,782
[soft music playing]

337
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:35,411
Auntie.

338
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:36,704
Diego.

339
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,456
How are you, Auntie? How's Ivy?

340
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,752
She still hasn't woken up.

341
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,382
I'm sorry about all this, Auntie.

342
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,845
I'm sorry I couldn't protect Ivy.

343
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:58,600
No, Diego.

344
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:00,978
Thank you…

345
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:04,273
because you were
planning Arnaldo's downfall.

346
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:09,069
Diego, thank you for not
abandoning my daughter.

347
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:13,949
[soft music playing]

348
00:17:19,413 --> 00:17:21,206
Auntie Camia, Ivy's tough.

349
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:26,128
I'm sure she'll get through this.

350
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:27,504
I know it.

351
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:31,508
And she won't let the Ardientes win.

352
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:35,763
[instrumental theme music playing]

353
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:49,860
[instrumental theme music playing]

354
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:01,914
Lily.

355
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:12,132
[instrumental theme music playing]

356
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:16,720
[whispering] Ivy's awake.

357
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:22,851
Lily?

358
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:31,026
[instrumental theme music playing]

359
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:40,327
Don't worry. We know now.

360
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:56,051
[instrumental theme music playing]

361
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:15,946
[instrumental theme music playing]

362
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,410
[music fades]

363
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:23,495
[reporter] <i>While Mayor Arnaldo Torillo</i>

364
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:24,872
<i>is now detained</i>
<i>here at the provincial jail,</i>

365
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:27,124
<i>the Ardiente</i>
<i>family says they are confident</i>

366
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:31,211
<i>the truth will come out</i>
<i>and he will soon be freed.</i>

367
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:33,338
[reporter] <i>Señor Julio,</i>
<i>do you have a message for</i>

368
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:34,756
<i>the people of Ardiente?</i>

369
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:39,595
<i>To the people of Ardiente,</i>
<i>your Señor Julio is calling upon you</i>

370
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:46,393
<i>to not believe hearsay from</i>
<i>our political rivals trying to ruin us.</i>

371
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:51,315
<i>My grandson did nothing wrong.</i>
<i>He is an innocent man.</i>

372
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,275
[reporter] <i>Is it true you threatened</i>

373
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:54,651
<i>the people who arrested the mayor?</i>

374
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:55,652
[Julio] <i>Let me tell you this,</i>

375
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:58,238
<i>everyone can understand</i>
<i>even the basics of the law.</i>

376
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:05,078
<i>You know that Arnaldo's arrest is illegal.</i>

377
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,247
<i>It is against the law!</i>

378
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:11,919
<i>But what did I do? I allowed it to happen.</i>

379
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:15,631
<i>Even when I knew it was wrong,</i>
<i>I allowed it to happen.</i>

380
00:20:15,714 --> 00:20:20,135
<i>Why? So that we can avoid even more chaos</i>

381
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:23,597
<i>that would have hurt</i>
<i>the people of Ardiente.</i>

382
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:27,392
<i>That's what's important to us--</i>
<i>everyone's safety.</i>

383
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:32,856
<i>Citizens of Ardiente, you are my children.</i>

384
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:37,986
<i>And I will always love you and put you</i>
<i>ahead of everything else.</i>

385
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:42,366
<i>That's why I sacrificed my own grandson.</i>

386
00:20:42,449 --> 00:20:44,910
<i>I let his arrest happen</i>

387
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:49,957
<i>so we could avoid more violence,</i>
<i>more chaos,</i>

388
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:55,879
<i>and more possibilities for the people</i>
<i>of Ardiente to get hurt.</i>

389
00:20:57,047 --> 00:21:01,885
<i>Now, if you will excuse us,</i>
<i>it has been a very taxing</i>

390
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:05,180
<i>and trying day for our family.</i>

391
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:11,395
I'm sure the Ardientes will
send people here to spy on us.

392
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:12,771
[exhales]

393
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:19,736
[tense music playing]

394
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,905
Thank you all for your concern,

395
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:27,577
but the Ardientes can't see
or know about us being together.

396
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:32,291
Mr. Pandoy, Miss Loring…

397
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:36,336
I'm sorry, but you need
to leave right away.

398
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:39,423
Jepoy, Anna…

399
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:42,509
go with them.

400
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:49,182
[tense music playing]

401
00:21:56,231 --> 00:21:57,691
You too, Mom.

402
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,570
You need to leave.

403
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,910
Attorney, I'll say it again.

404
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:14,082
I want Arnaldo out of
that stinking rathole

405
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,834
as soon as possible.

406
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:19,379
-Yes, Congressman.
-And please. Please!

407
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:22,841
Make sure the media doesn't get anything

408
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:27,220
that might tarnish our name,
especially not Arnaldo's.

409
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:29,222
Yes, Papa.

410
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:33,477
Now, please tell me…

411
00:22:34,436 --> 00:22:37,773
Who was behind all that bedlam?

412
00:22:38,774 --> 00:22:41,610
Papa, isn't it obvious?
It was Ivy and Diego

413
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:44,780
who staged everything
to bring Arnaldo down.

414
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:46,948
Hold on, Emilia. Are you sure about that?

415
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:49,242
Do you have proof to back up your claims?

416
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:51,036
[sighs] Come on, Raul.

417
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:54,664
Stop protecting and defending
your bastard son, already.

418
00:22:54,748 --> 00:22:55,957
It's so obvious!

419
00:22:56,041 --> 00:23:00,045
Papa, Diego came in right before
Arnaldo's little confession.

420
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,005
That was too timely!

421
00:23:02,089 --> 00:23:05,550
Plus, we should award Ivy
for the worst acting ever!

422
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:08,178
[sighs] It's like she didn't even try!

423
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:09,721
And, Papa,

424
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:12,516
they staged everything
in the grandest wedding.

425
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:15,185
It's obvious they plotted it

426
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:17,938
so everyone will see Arnaldo's downfall.

427
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,775
I must say, you have a point, Emilia.

428
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:25,695
But with our current situation…

429
00:23:28,323 --> 00:23:30,784
we can't be reckless.

430
00:23:30,867 --> 00:23:35,580
We cannot be carried away by our emotions.

431
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:40,627
We have to be sure because
the public's eyes are on us.

432
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:43,672
It's as if we're the bad guys.

433
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:47,259
So, if we are to hit back at anyone,

434
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:50,554
I want to make sure
we hit the right target.

435
00:23:50,637 --> 00:23:52,681
I need proof.

436
00:23:55,642 --> 00:23:56,893
[Julio sighs]

437
00:23:56,977 --> 00:24:00,105
Julio… you should see this.

438
00:24:03,233 --> 00:24:06,820
[tense music playing]

439
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:11,908
That's Arthur Vergara.
One of Camia Cruz's witnesses.

440
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:21,585
[tense music playing]

441
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:25,005
[music fades]

442
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:28,550
[somber music playing]

443
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:31,011
Mom, you have to leave too.

444
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:37,976
Whether you like it or not,
I'm not leaving.

445
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:40,687
Lily, you were shot!

446
00:24:41,646 --> 00:24:43,398
Arnaldo almost killed you!

447
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:47,527
Emilia tried to murder you!
What more reason do you need?

448
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:52,365
That wasn't the first attempt on my life,

449
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:54,201
and it certainly won't be the last.

450
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,871
What I'm doing is dangerous, Mom.

451
00:25:01,416 --> 00:25:03,501
You know that, right?

452
00:25:05,295 --> 00:25:06,838
When will all this be over?

453
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:11,134
When I bury your corpse?

454
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:17,057
The next time something
like this happens, remember…

455
00:25:18,725 --> 00:25:21,144
I'll be the one
to take the bullet for you.

456
00:25:21,228 --> 00:25:24,397
[tense music playing]

457
00:25:27,859 --> 00:25:29,027
[door closes]

458
00:25:31,112 --> 00:25:34,074
Hold on. Didn't he die? Bottled in a drum?

459
00:25:34,157 --> 00:25:35,784
Apparently not.

460
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:38,995
He was the one who leaked
Arnaldo's confession on live TV.

461
00:25:39,079 --> 00:25:43,500
[laughing]

462
00:25:45,085 --> 00:25:46,962
[laughing continues]

463
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:48,630
You mean to tell me

464
00:25:49,589 --> 00:25:55,387
that all it took to tarnish our name
was one crazy bastard?!

465
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:58,807
[Julio continues laughing]

466
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:04,145
How could we let this happen?!
Well?! How?!

467
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:12,404
How was a crazy person able
to make us all look stupid?!

468
00:26:13,196 --> 00:26:16,408
You. Come over here.

469
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:26,293
You have been the head of my
army for the past 16 years.

470
00:26:28,128 --> 00:26:30,338
How many times have you messed up?

471
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:33,508
Well? [scoffs]

472
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:38,638
Too many times to count.
That's why you can't answer me.

473
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:44,352
Congressman, I did my job well.
Do you remember Governor Alvarez

474
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:46,271
and that reporter you wanted dead?

475
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:48,523
-I did a clean job.
-[Julio scoffs]

476
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:53,028
Two examples from almost a lifetime ago!

477
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:58,033
And if my memory serves me right,
my rule is that

478
00:26:58,116 --> 00:27:01,453
you are only as good as your last job.

479
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:03,455
And if we look at it…

480
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:07,876
your last job was a mess

481
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:11,046
because you weren't able
to stop the public

482
00:27:11,129 --> 00:27:14,132
from barging into Arnaldo's wedding!

483
00:27:14,716 --> 00:27:18,094
What was wrong?! Tell me.
I gave you the weaponry!

484
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:24,225
I gave you the manpower!
I even gave you a chopper!

485
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:27,979
But what did you do?! What did you do?

486
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:31,816
Nothing! Zilch! Zero! Nada!

487
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:35,403
You were just running
around like a headless chicken!

488
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:38,323
You couldn't even hold back a crowd!

489
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:41,117
I am going to give you one last chance.

490
00:27:42,535 --> 00:27:46,164
Bring me the head of Arthur Vergara!

491
00:27:46,873 --> 00:27:51,669
Or else, I'll have
your head roll in the plaza!

492
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:53,838
Understood, Congressman.

493
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:56,800
You better be sure!

494
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:04,599
Now, these people think they can
just push our family around.

495
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,018
They're disrespecting us!

496
00:28:08,228 --> 00:28:10,230
Well, I want everyone to know…

497
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:15,151
no one in this world can bring me down.

498
00:28:16,152 --> 00:28:18,446
Not in a million years!

499
00:28:18,947 --> 00:28:21,533
And I want you to spread the news…

500
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:25,954
that Julio Ardiente is
coming down on them,

501
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:29,249
and I am coming down
on them with a vengeance!

502
00:28:29,791 --> 00:28:33,378
I am going to make it rain fire
and brimstone on them.

503
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:37,215
[Julio] <i>They'll regret the day</i>
<i>that they were born.</i>

504
00:28:44,305 --> 00:28:45,974
-Mom, let's go!
-Hurry up!

505
00:28:46,057 --> 00:28:49,310
There! That's where I last saw Arthur!

506
00:28:50,645 --> 00:28:52,772
Sir! Where's my payment?

507
00:28:53,314 --> 00:28:56,234
What are you talking about?
Scram! Search the house!

508
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:03,324
[suspenseful music playing]

509
00:29:10,248 --> 00:29:11,416
Sir, negative.

510
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:14,586
He escaped. Let's go.

511
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:19,966
Sir, he's not here. He was able to escape.

512
00:29:28,558 --> 00:29:29,601
[Arthur] <i>Ma'am Ivy.</i>

513
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:32,395
<i>Here's the 20 million pesos</i>
<i>of ransom money</i>

514
00:29:32,479 --> 00:29:35,148
<i>that Mayor Arnaldo paid me</i>
<i>for your release.</i>

515
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:38,818
<i>No one should make use of it</i>
<i>other than you.</i>

516
00:29:40,236 --> 00:29:43,531
<i>Thank you for the protection</i>
<i>you've given me.</i>

517
00:29:46,618 --> 00:29:49,996
Ma'am? Miss Aguas?

518
00:29:50,497 --> 00:29:51,539
Excuse me, ma'am.

519
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:54,959
Here are the documents
needed for our head office.

520
00:29:56,628 --> 00:30:00,757
Ma'am, I'm very sorry about
what happened to your wedding.

521
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:07,764
Irene, that's not part of your job.

522
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:10,683
So, let's not talk about it anymore.

523
00:30:11,017 --> 00:30:12,018
Yes, ma'am.

524
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:14,062
Open the bag.

525
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:22,612
Wow, Miss Aguas, that's a lot of money.

526
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:24,697
I want you to deposit
it all into the accounts

527
00:30:24,781 --> 00:30:28,827
of Shining Light Foundation,
New Home Orphanage,

528
00:30:28,910 --> 00:30:31,996
the Children's Hospital,
and Homes for the Aged.

529
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:34,958
-Under whose name, ma'am?
-Anonymous.

530
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:37,085
That's so kind of you, ma'am.

531
00:30:37,168 --> 00:30:38,753
Irene, that money isn't from me.

532
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:40,255
It was stolen by the Ardientes,

533
00:30:40,338 --> 00:30:42,549
so I'm returning it to the
people who deserve it.

534
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:45,009
You may go now.
Tell the guards to escort you.

535
00:30:45,093 --> 00:30:46,261
Okay, ma'am.

536
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:48,555
[Irene] Excuse me.

537
00:30:48,638 --> 00:30:50,765
[Emilia on TV] <i>Arnaldo, my son…</i>

538
00:30:52,267 --> 00:30:55,353
<i>Are you okay?</i>
<i>I'll be praying for you tonight.</i>

539
00:30:56,396 --> 00:30:57,981
[Emilia] <i>I'll visit you again</i>
<i>tomorrow, okay?</i>

540
00:31:03,862 --> 00:31:06,823
[Emilia] <i>As for your question earlier,</i>

541
00:31:06,906 --> 00:31:10,118
<i>yes, I will continue the rehabilitation</i>

542
00:31:10,201 --> 00:31:12,662
<i>and education programs for our inmates.</i>

543
00:31:12,745 --> 00:31:14,664
So, you're still committed
to public service

544
00:31:14,747 --> 00:31:16,291
despite what happened?

545
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:19,544
Of course I am. I'm a mother.

546
00:31:19,627 --> 00:31:26,676
<i>It's in my nature to care for others,</i>
<i>especially after seeing how terrible</i>

547
00:31:26,759 --> 00:31:28,928
their living conditions truly are.

548
00:31:29,012 --> 00:31:31,848
And as you can see,

549
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:35,268
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente
has no VIP treatment.

550
00:31:38,605 --> 00:31:39,606
Open it.

551
00:31:46,821 --> 00:31:48,156
Mayor, wake up.

552
00:31:49,699 --> 00:31:50,950
Come with me.

553
00:31:52,952 --> 00:31:54,871
[Emilia] <i>Please rest assured that</i>

554
00:31:56,414 --> 00:32:00,501
<i>we will not abuse our position</i>
<i>to gain privilege.</i>

555
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:07,967
[door opens]

556
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:14,557
<i>My son will be eating, bathing,</i>

557
00:32:14,641 --> 00:32:17,644
<i>and sharing a restroom</i>
<i>with all the other inmates here.</i>

558
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:29,364
Isn't that right, guys?

559
00:32:29,906 --> 00:32:32,367
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

560
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:34,327
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

561
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:48,383
Mayor. We need to return you
to the cell. You have a visitor.

562
00:32:53,846 --> 00:32:56,766
Ivy! Ivy, how are you?

563
00:32:56,849 --> 00:32:59,352
-Don't touch me.
-No. I'm so glad you're back!

564
00:32:59,435 --> 00:33:01,145
How's your wound? How are you?

565
00:33:01,229 --> 00:33:03,815
-I said don't touch me!
-Okay, okay, okay!

566
00:33:03,898 --> 00:33:05,817
I just want to make sure you're okay.

567
00:33:06,609 --> 00:33:07,819
I'm doing fine.

568
00:33:09,696 --> 00:33:13,950
Well, thank you for being here.
Thank you for visiting me.

569
00:33:14,033 --> 00:33:18,454
Thank you. I missed you.
I missed you so much!

570
00:33:18,538 --> 00:33:19,998
-You did?
-Yes.

571
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:22,875
[tense music playing]

572
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:26,045
I didn't come here to get
back together with you.

573
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:31,342
I came here to make sure
you'll go insane in this prison!

574
00:33:34,554 --> 00:33:37,765
I already regret what I did to Carlotta.
What more do you want?

575
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:38,933
This isn't enough!

576
00:33:39,934 --> 00:33:45,481
I want your conscience to eat at you.

577
00:33:46,065 --> 00:33:47,775
Will you ever forgive me?

578
00:33:49,235 --> 00:33:51,779
You don't know how it feels
to lose a mother.

579
00:33:53,948 --> 00:33:56,993
Would you like to experience it?
I can help you.

580
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:03,332
So you'll know the answer
to your question.

581
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:10,339
By the way, send my regards to Emilia.

582
00:34:11,215 --> 00:34:15,261
Given the fact that she wanted me killed,

583
00:34:15,344 --> 00:34:18,723
tell her it's only a matter of time

584
00:34:18,806 --> 00:34:21,017
before she gets what she's looking for.

585
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:24,020
Uh…

586
00:34:25,146 --> 00:34:26,481
What did Mom do to you?

587
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:28,649
You'll go insane here, Arnaldo.

588
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:33,529
What did Mom do to you? Wait! Ivy, please!

589
00:34:35,364 --> 00:34:36,574
<i>What did Mom do to you?</i>

590
00:34:38,743 --> 00:34:40,536
[stutters] Tell me. Tell me.

591
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:43,414
No, no. Ivy. Ivy! Ivy!

592
00:34:46,459 --> 00:34:48,336
Hey, call her for me! Ivy!

593
00:34:50,713 --> 00:34:51,798
Ivy, come back!

594
00:34:51,881 --> 00:34:57,386
Ivy! Ivy! Ivy! Ivy! Ivy!

595
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:04,435
[tense music playing]

596
00:35:16,656 --> 00:35:21,786
Ivy, come back here! Ivy! Ivy!

597
00:35:22,245 --> 00:35:25,123
[tense music playing]

598
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:26,666
How's my grandson?

599
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:28,960
Ivy! Ivy! Ivy!

600
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:31,379
-It's Arnaldo, Papa!
-[Arnaldo] Get off me!

601
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:36,884
[screaming] Ivy! Ivy! Ivy!

602
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:38,970
-[Emilia] Arnaldo?
-[Arnaldo screaming] Ivy!

603
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:42,974
Ivy! Ivy! Ivy! Ivy!

604
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:45,268
-[Emilia] Arnaldo?!
-[Arnaldo] Ivy!

605
00:35:45,351 --> 00:35:47,228
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!
-[Arnaldo] Let me go!

606
00:35:47,311 --> 00:35:50,731
Arnaldo! Let him go!
Let go of my son! Stop, stop!

607
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:53,276
Let go of me. I'm all right.
I'm okay. I'm okay.

608
00:35:53,359 --> 00:35:56,154
-That's enough! Stop it!
-[sobbing] I'm okay. I'm okay.

609
00:35:56,237 --> 00:35:59,115
Mom, get me out of here.

610
00:35:59,198 --> 00:36:02,243
-I'm here. I'm here.
-Get me out of here, Mom!

611
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:05,705
Please! Please let me out of here.

612
00:36:05,788 --> 00:36:07,165
I wanna make your life a living hell

613
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:10,376
because this is all your fault!
It's all your fault!

614
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:12,044
-[Julio] Arnaldo!
-It's all your fault!

615
00:36:12,128 --> 00:36:15,173
-[Emilia grunts]
-It's your fault too!

616
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:16,799
-[Julio] Arnaldo!
-I will kill you!

617
00:36:16,883 --> 00:36:19,385
I will kill you! I will kill you!

618
00:36:19,468 --> 00:36:20,386
-[Emilia] Papa!
-Ivy!

619
00:36:20,469 --> 00:36:22,471
-[Raul] Arnaldo, that's enough!
-[Julio] Arnaldo!

620
00:36:22,555 --> 00:36:27,768
[sobbing, screaming] Ivy! Ivy! Ivy! Ivy!

621
00:36:28,144 --> 00:36:31,147
-[stun gun sparks]
-[tense music playing]

622
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:33,900
[police officer] I'm sorry, ma'am.

623
00:36:33,983 --> 00:36:35,401
[Emilia gasps] Papa!

624
00:36:36,903 --> 00:36:38,905
I understand. I know you had to do it.

625
00:36:39,322 --> 00:36:40,615
[Raul] Sir, help us.

626
00:36:41,949 --> 00:36:42,700
[Emilia] Papa!

627
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:44,577
-Carry him to his cell.
-[Raul] Let's go.

628
00:36:45,411 --> 00:36:46,621
Are you okay?

629
00:36:46,704 --> 00:36:48,456
-[Emilia breathes heavily]
-[gate squeaks]

630
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:55,671
[tense music playing]

631
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,971
Papa, is he going to be okay?

632
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:06,807
[Julio stutters] Yeah, I think he is.

633
00:37:08,059 --> 00:37:09,644
Is he really going to stay here?

634
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:16,025
Such a miserable place!

635
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:23,491
[tense music playing]

636
00:37:25,451 --> 00:37:27,286
[phone ringing]

637
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:28,371
Hello?

638
00:37:29,038 --> 00:37:29,914
Mom?

639
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:32,208
Lily.

640
00:37:32,625 --> 00:37:36,712
Mom, I'm sorry it took me a while to call.

641
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:38,172
<i>It's okay, dear.</i>

642
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:40,258
What's important is I got
to hear your voice.

643
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:41,801
That's enough for me.

644
00:37:42,385 --> 00:37:43,970
<i>How are you, dear?</i>

645
00:37:44,053 --> 00:37:47,181
I really miss you.
When will I see you again?

646
00:37:48,140 --> 00:37:49,558
<i>I miss you too, Mom.</i>

647
00:37:49,642 --> 00:37:52,770
And don't worry.
We'll see each other soon.

648
00:37:53,729 --> 00:37:55,356
Very soon.

649
00:37:55,439 --> 00:37:58,943
Okay, then. Always take care of yourself.

650
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:05,074
[dramatic music playing]

651
00:38:05,157 --> 00:38:06,409
[music fades]

652
00:38:06,492 --> 00:38:07,868
See, Papa?

653
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:11,831
See? It's right there.
That CCTV footage won't lie.

654
00:38:11,914 --> 00:38:15,459
Ivy Aguas visited Arnaldo
before we came in.

655
00:38:15,543 --> 00:38:20,214
I wouldn't be surprised if that woman
slandered me to my son.

656
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:22,758
That's why Arnaldo's so mad at me.

657
00:38:22,842 --> 00:38:24,260
And he almost killed me!

658
00:38:26,762 --> 00:38:32,560
Well… You did try to
kill his fiancée, didn't you?

659
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:39,317
So, technically, your son's right
when he said this is your fault.

660
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:41,694
-What?!
-[scoffs] Come on, Emilia.

661
00:38:41,777 --> 00:38:43,571
From the very beginning,

662
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:48,242
you've tried to undermine
Ivy and Arnaldo's relationship.

663
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:54,332
And even though you knew
I wanted their wedding to continue,

664
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:56,125
you still disobeyed me.

665
00:38:56,208 --> 00:38:59,295
You actually tried to have Ivy killed.

666
00:39:00,629 --> 00:39:02,798
Excuse me, Papa. That's incorrect.

667
00:39:02,882 --> 00:39:05,092
I never admitted to being
behind the assassination

668
00:39:05,176 --> 00:39:06,135
plot against Ivy,

669
00:39:06,218 --> 00:39:09,180
so technically speaking,
I had nothing to do with that.

670
00:39:09,263 --> 00:39:10,348
[sarcastic chuckle]

671
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,352
You can lie to the public,

672
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:16,896
you can lie through your teeth…

673
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:19,982
but you can't lie to me.

674
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:24,653
I have eyes and ears all over my city.

675
00:39:25,613 --> 00:39:27,448
That's why I know the truth.

676
00:39:29,450 --> 00:39:30,451
Now…

677
00:39:31,911 --> 00:39:33,746
Do you have anything you want to say

678
00:39:34,413 --> 00:39:36,916
before I tell you your punishment?

679
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:39,418
Yes, Papa.

680
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:45,841
This is not about hatred
or jealousy towards Ivy Aguas.

681
00:39:46,509 --> 00:39:49,804
I can smell the traitor
in that woman, Papa.

682
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:52,932
She plotted everything
to bring Arnaldo down.

683
00:39:53,015 --> 00:39:54,892
I know that. I can feel it.

684
00:39:54,975 --> 00:39:58,229
Hunting down Arthur Vergara
is just a waste of time.

685
00:39:58,312 --> 00:39:59,855
We should get the head of the snake,

686
00:39:59,939 --> 00:40:03,317
and that's Ivy Aguas, Papa.
We should kill her!

687
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:05,820
We should kill her as early as now, Papa.

688
00:40:05,903 --> 00:40:07,947
Before the media finds her
and asks for an interview

689
00:40:08,030 --> 00:40:10,366
that can destroy our family's image!

690
00:40:11,325 --> 00:40:12,576
And if we do that, Papa?

691
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:15,788
You know that we can blame it
on our enemies, right?

692
00:40:16,622 --> 00:40:20,292
And with that, we might even get
the sympathy of the people.

693
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:22,336
Papa…

694
00:40:22,962 --> 00:40:27,216
Ivy Aguas is better off dead,
and you know it.

695
00:40:30,719 --> 00:40:31,762
[exhales sharply]

696
00:40:34,765 --> 00:40:38,269
[tense music playing]

697
00:40:40,229 --> 00:40:41,272
Do it.

698
00:40:41,355 --> 00:40:45,526
[tense music intensifies]

699
00:40:51,240 --> 00:40:54,368
Well? How did your meeting with Papa go?

700
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:57,455
You know, I can't believe
that you left me in there again!

701
00:40:57,955 --> 00:41:00,666
Why? What would I tell him
if I was there? [scoffs]

702
00:41:00,958 --> 00:41:03,961
Besides, Emilia, you did plan
to have Ivy killed, right?

703
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:06,589
You should be grateful
that I kept my mouth shut.

704
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:09,383
Well, that's what you are good at.

705
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:11,302
-Keeping your mouth shut.
-[Raul scoffs]

706
00:41:11,385 --> 00:41:14,597
At least some people
have the guts to defend me…

707
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:15,681
unlike you.

708
00:41:16,515 --> 00:41:22,605
Wait. Who are you referring to?
Jaguar? You think he's all that?

709
00:41:23,564 --> 00:41:26,275
You want the truth? Yes, it's Jaguar!

710
00:41:26,358 --> 00:41:28,777
You know, Raul, I wish you were Jaguar.

711
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:31,071
Maybe then you'd be able to say
and do something!

712
00:41:31,155 --> 00:41:32,448
Our family is falling apart.

713
00:41:32,531 --> 00:41:34,742
Our son is in jail,
but you're not doing anything.

714
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:36,869
All you do is just nothing! Nothing!

715
00:41:37,953 --> 00:41:39,121
Hold on, Emilia.

716
00:41:39,205 --> 00:41:41,790
Don't ever underestimate
the things I do for our family!

717
00:41:43,209 --> 00:41:45,711
What have you done for our family, Raul?

718
00:41:45,794 --> 00:41:48,506
Humor me. And if you keep pulling me down,

719
00:41:48,589 --> 00:41:50,758
I have no other choice but to dump you!

720
00:41:51,342 --> 00:41:54,136
I'm not done talking yet!
Are you threatening me?

721
00:41:54,553 --> 00:41:58,057
Do whatever you want, then!
I dare you, Emilia!

722
00:42:01,393 --> 00:42:04,188
[tense music playing]

723
00:42:15,699 --> 00:42:16,700
[sighs]

724
00:42:17,701 --> 00:42:21,121
People, I would like you
to meet the new head

725
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:26,001
of our private army,
Colonel Jose Ruel Sanggano.

726
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:29,213
Hello, ma'am. Hello, sir.

727
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:31,924
And I would like everybody else to know

728
00:42:32,007 --> 00:42:35,427
that we will be making
a lot of personnel changes.

729
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:38,180
So, for the rest of our staff…
Please sit down.

730
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:40,975
They better think twice,

731
00:42:41,058 --> 00:42:44,895
if they do not perform
according to my standards.

732
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:49,400
For your information,
Col. Sanggano used to lead

733
00:42:49,483 --> 00:42:52,194
the military operations
in the whole of Mindanao.

734
00:42:52,278 --> 00:42:54,280
That's why I am very confident in him.

735
00:42:55,114 --> 00:42:56,991
So, where's your former head, Papa?

736
00:42:57,616 --> 00:43:03,289
Emilia, you know how I treat
my men who are incompetent.

737
00:43:04,456 --> 00:43:10,588
I sent him on a vacation…
to the cemetery. [laughs]

738
00:43:10,796 --> 00:43:15,342
That is why my men have life insurance.

739
00:43:15,426 --> 00:43:17,720
Because I care for my people.

740
00:43:18,512 --> 00:43:21,640
I'm sure everyone is lining up
to work for you, Papa.

741
00:43:21,724 --> 00:43:23,559
It has always been the case.

742
00:43:24,143 --> 00:43:25,894
Thank you for joining us again, Colonel.

743
00:43:25,978 --> 00:43:27,104
Thank you, sir.

744
00:43:33,068 --> 00:43:34,361
[phone ringing]

745
00:43:35,863 --> 00:43:36,864
Boss?

746
00:43:36,947 --> 00:43:37,990
[Jaguar] <i>Jepoy.</i>

747
00:43:38,073 --> 00:43:39,533
Report to me immediately.

748
00:43:39,908 --> 00:43:41,660
<i>We have something to discuss.</i>

749
00:43:43,037 --> 00:43:43,954
All right, boss.

750
00:43:48,417 --> 00:43:51,545
Jepoy, where are you going?

751
00:43:56,216 --> 00:43:57,968
You and Miss Camia go ahead. I'll follow.

752
00:43:59,303 --> 00:44:01,972
-Where are you off to now?
-Anna, it's nothing.

753
00:44:03,098 --> 00:44:06,435
[unsettling music playing]

754
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:18,197
Anna, is Jepoy hiding something from us?

755
00:44:19,615 --> 00:44:20,616
No.

756
00:44:28,999 --> 00:44:32,544
[ominous music playing]

757
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:37,466
[beeps]

758
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:44,306
Some of my men saw you at Mayor
Arnaldo and Ivy Aguas' wedding.

759
00:44:45,015 --> 00:44:46,183
What were you doing there?

760
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:48,185
Simple, boss.

761
00:44:48,602 --> 00:44:52,356
I was going to kill Arnaldo,
but I didn't get the chance.

762
00:44:52,773 --> 00:44:55,734
I want to make him feel the
torture they made me go through.

763
00:44:56,610 --> 00:45:00,155
-Leave Mayor Arnaldo to me.
-Why, boss?

764
00:45:01,657 --> 00:45:03,283
Are we supposed to protect him?

765
00:45:03,367 --> 00:45:06,954
Do you know what happens
to those who question God?

766
00:45:09,039 --> 00:45:10,499
They get struck by lightning.

767
00:45:11,417 --> 00:45:15,671
And, in this place, I am God.
I am your God.

768
00:45:18,924 --> 00:45:20,926
-Boss.
-And this is my lightning bolt.

769
00:45:22,177 --> 00:45:24,346
You don't want to be struck
by lightning, do you?

770
00:45:24,430 --> 00:45:28,016
[suspenseful music playing]

771
00:45:30,185 --> 00:45:31,478
Understood, boss.

772
00:45:46,326 --> 00:45:52,291
[music intensifies]

773
00:46:14,771 --> 00:46:15,981
[police officer] This way, sir.

774
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:22,988
[melancholic music playing]

775
00:46:23,947 --> 00:46:24,948
[door opens]

776
00:46:34,791 --> 00:46:35,792
Clean him up.

777
00:46:36,877 --> 00:46:37,878
[door closes]

778
00:46:45,802 --> 00:46:46,803
[sighs]

779
00:46:48,639 --> 00:46:51,183
What happened to you, Arnaldo?

780
00:46:53,060 --> 00:46:58,398
You're the mayor of this city
and soon-to-be governor.

781
00:46:59,983 --> 00:47:04,655
Arnaldo! You were the
golden boy of our family.

782
00:47:05,531 --> 00:47:08,116
How could you let your life be ruined…

783
00:47:08,700 --> 00:47:10,410
by a woman?!

784
00:47:12,287 --> 00:47:14,414
Now, you just sit there and cry!

785
00:47:14,915 --> 00:47:16,917
Stop it! Wipe your tears.

786
00:47:17,709 --> 00:47:20,546
And be the man that I trained you to be!

787
00:47:23,840 --> 00:47:25,384
Arnaldo, please.

788
00:47:26,718 --> 00:47:28,971
Tell me what I can do to help you.

789
00:47:30,222 --> 00:47:32,599
Arnaldo, I will do anything. Anything!

790
00:47:33,350 --> 00:47:35,227
What do you want?! What do you need?!

791
00:47:37,563 --> 00:47:38,564
Ivy.

792
00:47:42,568 --> 00:47:44,027
Give me Ivy.

793
00:47:44,111 --> 00:47:47,406
[melancholic music playing]

794
00:47:47,698 --> 00:47:49,408
Give me Ivy.

795
00:47:50,409 --> 00:47:51,410
[sniffles]

796
00:47:52,369 --> 00:47:55,914
[sobbing] I'm begging you. Give me Ivy.

797
00:47:58,333 --> 00:48:02,379
Grandpa! I'm begging you.

798
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:06,091
[sobbing] Give me Ivy!

799
00:48:07,801 --> 00:48:10,053
I need Ivy!

800
00:48:12,556 --> 00:48:16,268
I can't live without her!

801
00:48:17,561 --> 00:48:21,815
That's all I need.
That's all I need in my life.

802
00:48:21,898 --> 00:48:25,569
She's all I need. [sobbing]

803
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:31,366
It's just really lonely here.

804
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:33,160
[breathing heavily]

805
00:48:33,243 --> 00:48:34,828
I need her in this bed.

806
00:48:34,911 --> 00:48:39,750
I want her. Here. With me.

807
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:43,211
Please, give her to me.

808
00:48:44,087 --> 00:48:50,135
It's really sad in this room,
and I need my wife here!

809
00:48:52,387 --> 00:48:56,266
If you really love me,
you will give her to me.

810
00:48:58,185 --> 00:48:59,853
Are you listening?

811
00:48:59,936 --> 00:49:02,189
You will give her to me.

812
00:49:02,272 --> 00:49:04,274
[sobs] Give her to me.

813
00:49:06,193 --> 00:49:07,486
Please!

814
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:13,617
[Arnaldo] Ivy…

815
00:49:14,618 --> 00:49:19,039
[melancholic music playing]

816
00:49:19,122 --> 00:49:24,961
No! No! No! [sobbing]

817
00:49:28,590 --> 00:49:30,467
[Julio] <i>I'm here</i>
<i>to make you an offer, Ivy.</i>

818
00:49:30,550 --> 00:49:32,386
<i>A hundred million pesos.</i>

819
00:49:32,469 --> 00:49:33,512
<i>In exchange for what?</i>

820
00:49:33,595 --> 00:49:34,554
<i>Get back together with my grandson.</i>

821
00:49:34,638 --> 00:49:35,806
[Camia] <i>What are you going to do?</i>

822
00:49:35,889 --> 00:49:39,643
<i>Are you going to help Arnaldo recover</i>
<i>after you tore him down?</i>

823
00:49:39,726 --> 00:49:42,229
<i>Arnaldo is the weakness of the Ardientes--</i>

824
00:49:42,312 --> 00:49:45,273
<i>Emilia, Raul, and especially Julio.</i>

825
00:49:45,357 --> 00:49:50,404
<i>So I need Arnaldo to finish off</i>
<i>the Ardientes once and for all.</i>

826
00:49:50,487 --> 00:49:52,948
<i>Let the games begin!</i>

827
00:49:53,031 --> 00:49:55,409
<i>Charges against Mayor Arnaldo Torillo</i>
<i>were dismissed.</i>

828
00:49:55,492 --> 00:49:58,745
[Camia] <i>They've proven yet again</i>
<i>that they have the law at their disposal.</i>

829
00:49:58,829 --> 00:49:59,579
[thuds]

830
00:50:00,664 --> 00:50:03,750
[theme music playing]
